      "questions": {
        "addressed": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Is the specific requirement of `anchor.statement` present in `item.text`? The requirement is that the sprint bead names the crate and layer each change lands in, and that layer is the lowest layer whose crates all use the change. Examples of presence: 'puts the retry helper in sc-agent-types, layer 1, because both sc-anthropic and sc-openai use it', 'lands in sc-llm (layer 2), the lowest layer used by all callers'. Being about the same area, or doing the opposite, is not presence. A bare mention of the topic, or a plan to work on it, without the specific content is no, not unclear.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The requirement is present in the item text, in any wording.",
            "no": "The requirement is absent from the item text.",
            "unclear": "Something resembling the requirement appears, but whether it is the requirement cannot be determined."
          }
        },
        "contradicted": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Does `item.text` plan something that breaks `anchor.statement` (the sprint bead names the crate and layer each change lands in, and that layer is the lowest layer whose crates all use the change)? Breaking it means, for example: placing shared code in a higher crate and copying it to siblings, placing a change used by several crates above the lowest common layer, or not placing code by layer at all while duplicating it. Silence about the requirement is not a conflict, and an item that merely does not mention it answers no. Judge conflict only.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item plans something that breaks the requirement, for example: placing shared code in a higher crate and copying it to siblings, placing a change used by several crates above the lowest common layer, or not placing code by layer at all while duplicating it.",
            "no": "Nothing in the item breaks the requirement, whether or not the item mentions it.",
            "unclear": "The item plans something that might break the requirement, but the text does not settle it."
          }
        },
        "relevant": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "`anchor.scope` names the work this anchor governs: code changes in crates under crates/ and which crate and layer each change lands in. Decide whether the planning item in `item.text` plans or changes that work, directly or as a stated prerequisite. Do not judge compliance or conflict. An item that only documents, describes, reviews or plans this subject still touches it.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item plans or changes code changes in crates under crates/ and which crate and layer each change lands in.",
            "no": "The item plans other work; code changes in crates under crates/ and which crate and layer each change lands in is not part of it.",
            "unclear": "It cannot be told from the item text what part of the system it changes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
